doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23901119"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergeyChere/colorsplit-nqueens"
keywords:
  - n-queens
  - OEIS A000170
  - exact counting
  - meet-in-the-middle
  - GPU
  - CUDA
abstract: >-
  Exact counting of the solutions Q(n) of the n-queens problem by splitting the board into
  white and black squares: the two colors interact only through rows and columns, so Q(n)
  is a sum of table lookups on an exact key. CPU versions in C and Java, a CUDA version for
  GPUs, tools to check and merge checkpoint files, and the 4096 partial sums of Q(25), Q(26), Q(27) and of
  the new value Q(28) = 2564269152506723832.
